@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ito-il27-nouns`
IMPORT `ito-il27-tax-years`
IMPORT `ito-s39a-discharged-soldier`
IMPORT `ito-credit-points-published-figures`

-- ===========================================================================
-- Tests for s 39A. Row IL-27. Expected values worked by hand from lines 1610-1617 before the rules were run; none edited to
-- match the code. A month is a calendar month; the month of discharge is not counted; the 36 months follow it.
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Tests — section 39A`

-- The fields, in order: tax year; Israeli resident; sex; a discharged soldier; full months of service; year of discharge;
-- month of discharge; foreign worker.
GIVEN `the year`    IS A NUMBER
      `resident`    IS A BOOLEAN
      `sex`         IS A `A person's sex, for these sections`
      `served`      IS A NUMBER
      `the end month` IS A NUMBER
      `the end year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
`in` `the year` `, resident:` `resident` `; a soldier of sex` `sex` `who served` `served` `full months and was discharged in month` `the end month` `of` `the end year` MEANS
    `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A` OF `the year`, `resident`, `sex`, TRUE, `served`, `the end year`, `the end month`, FALSE

-- The same, but not a discharged soldier within the Law (a), or a foreign worker (b).
GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
`not a discharged soldier, in` `the year` MEANS
    `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A` OF `the year`, TRUE, `a man`, FALSE, 24, 2025, 3, FALSE

GIVEN `the year` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A`
`a foreign worker, in` `the year` MEANS
    `A discharged soldier in a tax year, for section 39A` OF `the year`, TRUE, `a man`, TRUE, 24, 2025, 3, TRUE

§§ `The fraction by sex and months served`

-- A man who served 24 months (at least 23): one sixth for each month. Discharged in March 2025: the 36 months are April 2025 to
-- March 2028. Tax year 2026 lies wholly inside: 12 x 1/6 = 2.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
-- Tax year 2025: April to December, 9 months x 1/6 = 1.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2025 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 3/2
-- Tax year 2028: January to March, 3 months x 1/6 = 0.5.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2028 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 1/2
-- Tax years 2029 (after the 36 months) and 2024 (before discharge): nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2029 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2024 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 0
-- A man who served 22 months (less than 23): one twelfth. 2026: 12 x 1/12 = 1.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 22 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 1
-- Both sides of the man's threshold: 23 gives one sixth (2), 22 one twelfth (1).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 23 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
-- A woman: 22 full months or more is one sixth (2); 21 is one twelfth (1).
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a woman` `who served` 22 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a woman` `who served` 21 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 1
-- The same 22 months for a man is less than his 23: one twelfth.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 22 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 1

§§ `The edges of the 36 months`

-- Discharged in December 2025: the 36 months are January 2026 to December 2028. 2026 is the first year, whole: 12 x 1/6 = 2; 2025: 0.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 30 `full months and was discharged in month` 12 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2025 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 30 `full months and was discharged in month` 12 `of` 2025) EQUALS 0
-- Discharged in December 2023: January 2024 to December 2026. 2024 whole (2); 2027 nothing.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2024 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 30 `full months and was discharged in month` 12 `of` 2023) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2027 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 30 `full months and was discharged in month` 12 `of` 2023) EQUALS 0
-- Discharged in January 2025: the 36 months are February 2025 to January 2028. 2025: 11 months; 2028: 1 month. At 1/12: 11/12 and 1/12.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2025 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 12 `full months and was discharged in month` 1 `of` 2025) EQUALS 11/12
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2028 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 12 `full months and was discharged in month` 1 `of` 2025) EQUALS 1/12

§§ `Not a discharged soldier; tax year; foreign worker`

#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`not a discharged soldier, in` 2026) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2023 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2022) BECAUSE "row IL-27 does not hold the text of these sections for a tax year before 2024"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 39A for` (`a foreign worker, in` 2026) BECAUSE "section 48A and the regulations made under it are not encoded in this model"
-- A foreign worker with no points in the year (2029) has nothing for s 48A to take away.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`a foreign worker, in` 2029) EQUALS 0

§§ `Fork F1 — the section names no residence condition`

-- A non-resident with 2 points on the text: the default declines.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) BECAUSE "sections 39A, 39B, 40A and 40B name no residence condition, and here residence decides"
-- The readings by name.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A, reading the residence condition as` `no residence condition` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A, reading the residence condition as` `an Israeli resident only` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` FALSE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A, reading the residence condition as` `an Israeli resident only` `, for` (`in` 2026 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 2
-- Where the points are nil the readings agree, and the default answers.
#ASSERT `the credit points under section 39A for` (`in` 2029 `, resident:` FALSE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) EQUALS 0
-- The default reading is declined where residence decides.
#ASSERT `the reading row IL-27 takes of the sections that name no residence condition` EQUALS `declined where residence decides`

§§ `The credit in NIS`

-- The Tax Authority's published value of a credit point for 2025 is 2,904 (row IL-01, itc135-2025 p. 4). A man discharged after 24 months in
-- March 2025: 1.5 points in 2025 (9 months x 1/6): 1.5 x 2,904 = 4,356.
#ASSERT `the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025 EQUALS 2904
#ASSERT `the credit under section 39A, in NIS, for` (`in` 2025 `, resident:` TRUE `; a soldier of sex` `a man` `who served` 24 `full months and was discharged in month` 3 `of` 2025) `, at a credit-point value of` (`the value of one credit point published by the Israel Tax Authority for tax year` 2025) EQUALS 4356
